+   "setPageFavorite" ["Add or remove a favourite" "Adds the page page-id names (its UUID, or a page's or journal's title; a tag or property by its UUID) to the sidebar's Favorites list with favorite=true, or removes it with favorite=false. A new favourite is appended at the bottom of the list, unlike the app, which adds a new favourite at the top. Add takes a page, journal, tag or property, built-in ones included while visible, as the app's page menu does; a remove takes every slot linking the page, duplicates included, and never touches the page itself. Re-sends are no-ops answering 200 and writing nothing: result already a favourite on an add, was not a favourite on a remove. Refuses, writing nothing and naming page-id or the field: with 404 an id that names nothing, or something hidden; with 400 (add only) a page in the Recycle bin (a remove by UUID clears a favourite deletePage left behind; deletePage hides a favourite and restoring the page brings it back), a block (only pages can be favourites), an asset or a page whose name is a UUID; with 400 any body field but favorite and dry-run, and a favorite that isn't true or false; with 409 a title several pages share (candidates names them) or, when the graph has no favourites page and something else holds its name, $$$favorites under an unexpected uuid. When the graph has no favourites page an add creates it as a new graph has it, in the same transaction. Every write is one transaction, read back before it is committed (500, with nothing written, when the list wouldn't hold what was asked). Returns result (added, removed, already a favourite or was not a favourite), the page, and the whole list as listFavorites returns it. With dry-run=true in the body the same checks and write run on a throwaway copy of the graph and the same answer comes back with dry-run: true, with nothing written. Unavailable for E2EE graphs (400): the favourites page and its blocks are encrypted."]
+   "reorderFavorites" ["Reorder the favourites" "Puts the sidebar's Favorites list in the order page-ids gives. Pass the full list, every favourite once, in the new order: call listFavorites first and reorder what it returns (a page or journal by its UUID or title, a journal also by its YYYY-MM-DD date; a tag, property or block by its UUID). Anything else is refused with one 400 that names every problem, writing nothing: an entry that is not a favourite (or names nothing, or something hidden or in the Recycle bin), an entry that is a duplicate of an earlier one (by UUID or by title), every favourite missing from the list, an entry that isn't a string, and any body field but page-ids and dry-run. As the app does, each favourite slot keeps its place and its order keys are unchanged: the first slots that link a visible page, one per favourite, are re-pointed at the pages they should now hold, so a later duplicate slot that sat among them may now link another page and stays behind its page's slot. Slots that link nothing or a page that is hidden or in the Recycle bin, and the later duplicates after those first slots, are kept as they are, and a slot is never deleted, so a reorder removes nothing. The current order, and an empty list on a graph with no favourites, answer the list and write nothing. Every write is one transaction, read back before it is committed (500, with nothing written, when the list wouldn't be in the order given). Returns the whole list as listFavorites returns it. With dry-run=true in the body the same checks and write run on a throwaway copy of the graph and the same answer comes back with dry-run: true, with nothing written. Unavailable for E2EE graphs (400): the favourites page and its blocks are encrypted."]
    "createTag" ["Create a tag" "Creates a Logseq tag with the supplied title and, in the same transaction, the tags it extends and its tag properties, and returns the tag with both. Each extends entry is a tag and each properties entry a visible property, by UUID, ident or title; anything else (such as a page with that title), and a built-in tag the app hides from its extends picker (Tag, Page, Journal, Property, Query, Template and the like), is refused, naming the entry, and nothing is created. Refuses with 409 and writes nothing when a page, journal, tag or property already uses the title, compared case-insensitively as Logseq compares page names (so #Movie and #movie are the same title); the error names each one's kind, title and UUID, so there is no need to search before creating. An existing page is not converted into a tag: when a page promotePageToTag would accept holds the title, the error says to call promote_page_to_tag with that page's UUID, which turns it into a tag keeping its blocks and references, and its existing entry has promote: true. Not checked on E2EE graphs, whose names are ciphertext."]
    "getTag" ["Get a tag" "Returns one tag by UUID or ident (as updateTag takes it), with the tags it extends and its tag properties. Answers 404 for an id that names no visible tag."]
    "listTagObjects" ["List objects with a tag" "Returns a cursor-paginated flat list of blocks and pages tagged with the addressed tag. Results are not recursively expanded."]
